  "strategy": "We are to minimize the evaluation function:  \n    `evaluate_sequence(sequence)` = 2 * n * max(convolve(a,a)) / (sum_a)**2  \n\nThe problem is to find a sequence of non-negative coefficients whose normalized self-convolution has the smallest peak.\n\nOur Approach:\nWe'll use a Genetic Algorithm (GA) with crossover and mutation to search over sequences of fixed length (1000). The search will include:\n1. Initialization based on provided parent sequence (if available)\n2.Generation of new candidates through uniform crossover and adaptive mutation\n\nDetails:\n- We keep a population of 25 sequences of length 1000\n- Each generation, we evaluate the fitness (objective) of all population members\n- We generate 5 new candidates: one from mutation of the best candidate and four from uniform crossover between random parents\n- The best candidates (lowest fitness) are selected for the next generation based on their performance\n\nImplementation Steps:\n\n1. Initialization:\n   - Load parent if available and normalize it\n   - Generate 24 normalized random sequences to form the initial population\n\n2.Evaluation:\n   - For each candidate, call `evaluate_sequence(sequence)` and record the fitness\n   - Safeguard against sequences with too small sum (due to clipping) - `evaluate_sequence` handles this\n\n3.Mutation:\n   - For the best candidate, apply Gaussian perturbation to each coefficient\n   - Clip to non-negative values and normalize (if sum too small, normalize to trace conditions of evaluator)\n\n4.Crossover:\n   - Between two parent sequences, create new candidate by randomly choosing which parent contributes to each gene\n   - Normalize the result\n\n5.Selection:\n   - Evaluate the new candidates\n   - Combine old and new population (30 total), remove duplicates, and sort by fitness\n   - Keep the best 25 for the next generation\n\n6.Loop:\n   - Run for up to 5000 generations (each candidate takes ~0.01 seconds, so max 50 evaluations/sec)\n   - Print results periodically\n   - If fitness drops below 1.5027, we return the candidate and stop\n\n7.Fallback:\n   - Return the best candidate found within the time limit",
